1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:02,001
What's today's video about?

2
00:00:02,001 --> 00:00:05,254
We're covering Minna no Nihongo N4 grammar today!

3
00:00:05,254 --> 00:00:09,619
It looks challenging, but I'll do my best!

4
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: Ordering at a Café

5
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:15,101
This café is so beautiful!

6
00:00:15,125 --> 00:00:19,225
Yeah, let's check out the menu.

7
00:00:19,248 --> 00:00:23,315
There are drinks and sweets.

8
00:00:23,338 --> 00:00:27,333
I'd like some coffee.

9
00:00:27,357 --> 00:00:31,290
I'll go with tea.

10
00:00:31,313 --> 00:00:34,946
What about sweets?

11
00:00:34,969 --> 00:00:38,236
They have cake.

12
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:42,793
Chocolate cake and cheesecake.

13
00:00:42,816 --> 00:00:46,249
Which one is tastier?

14
00:00:46,272 --> 00:00:50,306
The chocolate cake is really popular.

15
00:00:50,329 --> 00:00:53,395
Then I'll have that.

16
00:00:53,418 --> 00:00:57,492
I'll take the cheesecake.

17
00:00:57,516 --> 00:01:01,858
Excuse me, may we order?

18
00:01:01,881 --> 00:01:06,348
One coffee and one tea, please.

19
00:01:06,371 --> 00:01:12,476
And also a chocolate cake and a cheesecake, please.

20
00:01:12,499 --> 00:01:15,651
Let's wait a moment.

21
00:01:15,675 --> 00:01:19,575
Oh, the cakes are here!

22
00:01:19,598 --> 00:01:22,113
Let's dig in!

23
00:01:22,136 --> 00:01:25,896
How's the chocolate cake?

24
00:01:25,919 --> 00:01:29,454
It's really sweet.

25
00:01:29,478 --> 00:01:31,747
And delicious!

26
00:01:31,770 --> 00:01:34,368
I'm glad you like it!

27
00:01:34,392 --> 00:01:38,144
How's the cheesecake?

28
00:01:38,167 --> 00:01:42,334
This is delicious too!

29
00:01:42,357 --> 00:01:47,336
Next time, I want to try the cheesecake.

30
00:01:47,359 --> 00:01:50,460
Let's come here again!

31
00:01:50,484 --> 00:01:54,251
Yes, let's do that!

32
00:01:54,274 --> 00:01:55,774
Scene 2: Choosing a Room – Ocean View or Mountain View?

33
00:01:55,774 --> 00:02:01,074
Excuse me, I'd like to book a room.

34
00:02:01,096 --> 00:02:04,196
Certainly, thank you!

35
00:02:04,219 --> 00:02:10,119
We have rooms with ocean views and mountain views.

36
00:02:10,142 --> 00:02:13,936
Which one would you prefer?

37
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:18,193
I'm not sure which one is better.

38
00:02:18,216 --> 00:02:23,250
The ocean-view rooms have amazing scenery.

39
00:02:23,273 --> 00:02:26,939
What about the mountain-view rooms?

40
00:02:26,962 --> 00:02:31,474
The mountain-view rooms are very quiet.

41
00:02:31,498 --> 00:02:36,202
I want to rest in a quiet room.

42
00:02:36,226 --> 00:02:41,059
In that case, how about a mountain-view room?

43
00:02:41,082 --> 00:02:44,640
Are the ocean-view rooms noisy?

44
00:02:44,664 --> 00:02:49,330
You can hear the sound of waves a little.

45
00:02:49,353 --> 00:02:52,865
I'm sensitive to noise.

46
00:02:52,889 --> 00:02:56,522
Do you want to sleep well at night?

47
00:02:56,545 --> 00:03:00,379
Yes, I want to sleep soundly.

48
00:03:00,402 --> 00:03:04,236
Then I think the mountain-view room would be better.

49
00:03:04,259 --> 00:03:07,993
Are the rooms the same size?

50
00:03:08,016 --> 00:03:11,282
Yes, they're the same size.

51
00:03:11,305 --> 00:03:14,774
What's the size of the bed like?

52
00:03:14,798 --> 00:03:18,465
Both are large beds.

53
00:03:18,488 --> 00:03:22,188
Is there a price difference?

54
00:03:22,211 --> 00:03:26,644
The ocean-view room is slightly more expensive.

55
00:03:26,667 --> 00:03:28,866
I see.

56
00:03:28,889 --> 00:03:33,023
The mountain-view room is cheaper, though.

57
00:03:33,046 --> 00:03:36,552
I don’t mind not having a view.

58
00:03:36,575 --> 00:03:40,958
Shall I book the mountain-view room for you, then?

59
00:03:40,981 --> 00:03:45,580
Yes. How do I make the reservation?

60
00:03:45,604 --> 00:03:49,907
Please write your name on this form.

61
00:03:49,931 --> 00:03:53,275
Okay, I’ve written it.

62
00:03:53,298 --> 00:03:55,468
Thank you very much.

63
00:03:55,491 --> 00:03:59,624
I’d like the mountain-view room, please.

64
00:03:59,647 --> 00:04:01,147
Scene 3: How to Choose Between Shinkansen and Local Trains

65
00:04:01,147 --> 00:04:06,144
Excuse me, may I ask you something?

66
00:04:06,168 --> 00:04:09,354
Of course, what is it?

67
00:04:09,378 --> 00:04:15,212
I want to go to Kyoto. How should I get there?

68
00:04:15,235 --> 00:04:20,551
You have the Shinkansen and the rapid train.

69
00:04:20,574 --> 00:04:23,841
Which one is faster?

70
00:04:23,864 --> 00:04:28,197
The Shinkansen is faster.

71
00:04:28,220 --> 00:04:32,900
How long does the Shinkansen take?

72
00:04:32,923 --> 00:04:36,190
About 15 minutes.

73
00:04:36,214 --> 00:04:39,529
What about the rapid train?

74
00:04:39,552 --> 00:04:43,419
It takes about 40 minutes.

75
00:04:43,442 --> 00:04:46,997
How about the price?

76
00:04:47,020 --> 00:04:51,120
The rapid train is cheaper.

77
00:04:51,143 --> 00:04:54,609
I’m not in a hurry.

78
00:04:54,632 --> 00:04:59,184
Then how about taking the rapid train?

79
00:04:59,208 --> 00:05:03,179
I’d like to enjoy the scenery along the way.

80
00:05:03,202 --> 00:05:08,506
You can see beautiful views from the rapid train.

81
00:05:08,529 --> 00:05:12,629
Alright, I’ll take the rapid train.

82
00:05:12,652 --> 00:05:16,752
You can buy the ticket over there.

83
00:05:16,775 --> 00:05:21,142
I don’t know how to buy a ticket.

84
00:05:21,166 --> 00:05:24,799
Shall I show you how?

85
00:05:24,822 --> 00:05:27,489
Yes, please.

86
00:05:27,511 --> 00:05:32,102
First, press this button.

87
00:05:32,126 --> 00:05:34,646
Pressed it.

88
00:05:34,669 --> 00:05:38,903
Next, insert the money.

89
00:05:38,926 --> 00:05:42,359
I’ve inserted 1,000 yen.

90
00:05:42,382 --> 00:05:46,252
Now press the Kyoto button.

91
00:05:46,276 --> 00:05:49,576
Okay, this one, right?

92
00:05:49,599 --> 00:05:53,265
Your ticket and change will come out.

93
00:05:53,288 --> 00:05:55,662
Here it comes.

94
00:05:55,686 --> 00:05:58,066
Thank you very much.

95
00:05:58,089 --> 00:06:01,623
Have a safe trip!

96
00:06:01,646 --> 00:06:03,146
Scene 4: Consultation on Choosing a Shirt

97
00:06:03,146 --> 00:06:08,479
Excuse me, I’m looking for a shirt.

98
00:06:08,502 --> 00:06:10,935
Welcome. How can I help you?

99
00:06:10,958 --> 00:06:14,025
What kind of shirt are you looking for?

100
00:06:14,048 --> 00:06:19,515
I want to wear it to my friend’s wedding.

101
00:06:19,538 --> 00:06:22,471
I see.

102
00:06:22,494 --> 00:06:27,194
I'm not sure which shirt to choose.

103
00:06:27,217 --> 00:06:31,526
How about this white shirt?

104
00:06:31,549 --> 00:06:35,816
White feels a little plain.

105
00:06:35,839 --> 00:06:40,555
Then, how about this blue shirt?

106
00:06:40,578 --> 00:06:44,845
Blue is nice and pretty.

107
00:06:44,868 --> 00:06:50,135
I think it would suit you.

108
00:06:50,159 --> 00:06:53,939
Which size should I pick?

109
00:06:53,962 --> 00:06:57,929
Should I go for a slightly larger size?

110
00:06:57,952 --> 00:07:02,052
No, a perfect fit would be better.

111
00:07:02,075 --> 00:07:06,412
How about the M size, then?

112
00:07:06,436 --> 00:07:09,821
Can I try it on?

113
00:07:09,844 --> 00:07:14,478
Yes, you can try it on over there.

114
00:07:14,501 --> 00:07:17,334
I tried it on.

115
00:07:17,357 --> 00:07:19,524
How does it look?

116
00:07:19,547 --> 00:07:22,931
It looks great!

117
00:07:22,955 --> 00:07:26,821
I’d also like to buy a tie.

118
00:07:26,844 --> 00:07:30,744
What color do you like?

119
00:07:30,767 --> 00:07:35,124
I’m looking for a red tie.

120
00:07:35,148 --> 00:07:38,481
How about this one?

121
00:07:38,504 --> 00:07:42,171
Would it go well with the blue shirt?

122
00:07:42,194 --> 00:07:47,060
Yes, it would match perfectly!

123
00:07:47,083 --> 00:07:50,550
What about pants?

124
00:07:50,573 --> 00:07:54,273
Black pants would be a good choice.

125
00:07:54,296 --> 00:07:57,996
I already have black pants.

126
00:07:58,019 --> 00:08:02,765
So, just the shirt and tie then?

127
00:08:02,789 --> 00:08:06,256
Yes, I’ll take these.

128
00:08:06,279 --> 00:08:09,912
Thank you very much.

129
00:08:09,935 --> 00:08:11,435
Scene 5: Menu Consultation

130
00:08:11,435 --> 00:08:13,802
Excuse me.

131
00:08:13,825 --> 00:08:17,891
Could I see the menu, please?

132
00:08:17,914 --> 00:08:21,348
Here you go.

133
00:08:21,371 --> 00:08:26,482
Could you recommend something delicious?

134
00:08:26,505 --> 00:08:30,805
Our curry is very popular.

135
00:08:30,828 --> 00:08:35,900
I’m not good with spicy food, though.

136
00:08:35,924 --> 00:08:38,698
I see.

137
00:08:38,722 --> 00:08:42,855
How about something not spicy?

138
00:08:42,878 --> 00:08:47,545
In that case, how about omurice?

139
00:08:47,568 --> 00:08:51,501
Is omurice sweet?

140
00:08:51,524 --> 00:08:55,895
Yes, it has a mild flavor.

141
00:08:55,919 --> 00:08:59,632
Are the portions large?

142
00:08:59,655 --> 00:09:03,768
Yes, they’re quite big.

143
00:09:03,791 --> 00:09:08,937
I don’t eat much, though.

144
00:09:08,961 --> 00:09:13,665
We can make it half-size for you.

145
00:09:13,688 --> 00:09:17,844
How do I order that?

146
00:09:17,867 --> 00:09:22,741
Just say, 'Half portion, please.'

147
00:09:22,764 --> 00:09:25,319
Got it.

148
00:09:25,342 --> 00:09:28,676
Would you like soup with that?

149
00:09:28,699 --> 00:09:32,166
How’s the soup?

150
00:09:32,189 --> 00:09:36,855
Our tomato soup is highly recommended.

151
00:09:36,878 --> 00:09:40,145
I love tomatoes.

152
00:09:40,168 --> 00:09:42,963
Would you like a salad too?

153
00:09:42,987 --> 00:09:47,087
What kind of salad is it?

154
00:09:47,110 --> 00:09:51,429
It's a salad with eggs and vegetables.

155
00:09:51,453 --> 00:09:54,561
Is the portion large?

156
00:09:54,584 --> 00:09:58,451
No, it's small.

157
00:09:58,474 --> 00:10:02,177
Then, I'll have the salad too, please.

158
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:04,904
Certainly.

159
00:10:04,927 --> 00:10:10,861
I'd like half an omurice, soup, and a salad, please.

160
00:10:10,883 --> 00:10:13,950
I'll bring them right away.

161
00:10:13,973 --> 00:10:15,473
Scene 6: Exploring the Museum / A Rainy Day Museum Visit

162
00:10:15,473 --> 00:10:18,906
It's raining today.

163
00:10:18,929 --> 00:10:23,596
Yeah, what should we do for sightseeing?

164
00:10:23,619 --> 00:10:28,452
Walking outside seems tough in this weather.

165
00:10:28,475 --> 00:10:32,542
True, I don’t want to get soaked.

166
00:10:32,565 --> 00:10:36,865
Is there a way to sightsee without getting wet?

167
00:10:36,888 --> 00:10:41,388
How about visiting a museum?

168
00:10:41,411 --> 00:10:45,288
Are museums interesting?

169
00:10:45,311 --> 00:10:50,228
Yes, you can learn about Japanese history.

170
00:10:50,252 --> 00:10:53,324
Is it far from the station?

171
00:10:53,347 --> 00:10:57,318
It takes about 20 minutes on foot.

172
00:10:57,341 --> 00:11:01,895
I don’t want to walk in the rain.

173
00:11:01,918 --> 00:11:04,985
You should take the bus instead.

174
00:11:05,008 --> 00:11:08,241
Where’s the bus stop?

175
00:11:08,264 --> 00:11:11,441
It’s in front of the station.

176
00:11:11,465 --> 00:11:14,821
Does the bus come often?

177
00:11:14,844 --> 00:11:18,110
One comes every 10 minutes.

178
00:11:18,133 --> 00:11:21,315
That’s convenient!

179
00:11:21,339 --> 00:11:25,372
What should we do after the museum?

180
00:11:25,395 --> 00:11:28,862
Is there a café nearby?

181
00:11:28,885 --> 00:11:33,034
There’s a café inside the museum.

182
00:11:33,057 --> 00:11:36,490
How about resting there?

183
00:11:36,513 --> 00:11:38,846
Sounds good!

184
00:11:38,869 --> 00:11:41,136
Let’s do that.

185
00:11:41,159 --> 00:11:45,660
Can we have lunch there too?

186
00:11:45,684 --> 00:11:49,917
Yes, they have delicious sandwiches.

187
00:11:49,940 --> 00:11:53,010
I’m looking forward to it!

188
00:11:53,033 --> 00:11:57,533
Okay, let’s head to the bus stop first.

189
00:11:57,556 --> 00:12:01,223
You should bring an umbrella.

190
00:12:01,246 --> 00:12:03,391
Good idea.

191
00:12:03,414 --> 00:12:07,381
We might get a little wet walking to the bus stop.

192
00:12:07,404 --> 00:12:10,377
Did we forget anything?

193
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:13,100
I think we’re good.

194
00:12:13,123 --> 00:12:15,223
Let’s go!

195
00:12:15,246 --> 00:12:16,746
Scene 7: Getting to the Airport / Your Guide to Narita Airport

196
00:12:16,746 --> 00:12:19,213
Excuse me.

197
00:12:19,236 --> 00:12:22,947
I’d like to go to the airport.

198
00:12:22,970 --> 00:12:25,237
Got it.

199
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:28,293
Which airport are you heading to?

200
00:12:28,316 --> 00:12:31,896
Narita Airport.

201
00:12:31,920 --> 00:12:35,072
That’s quite far.

202
00:12:35,095 --> 00:12:39,161
How long does it take to get there?

203
00:12:39,184 --> 00:12:43,823
About 2 hours by regular roads.

204
00:12:43,846 --> 00:12:47,993
I’d like to get there faster.

205
00:12:48,017 --> 00:12:51,917
You should take the expressway.

206
00:12:51,940 --> 00:12:56,006
How long does it take on the highway?

207
00:12:56,029 --> 00:12:59,610
About an hour.

208
00:12:59,634 --> 00:13:02,774
That's fast!

209
00:13:02,797 --> 00:13:07,830
But there's a toll fee.

210
00:13:07,853 --> 00:13:10,532
How much is the toll?

211
00:13:10,556 --> 00:13:14,027
Around 2,000 yen.

212
00:13:14,050 --> 00:13:17,283
Please take the highway.

213
00:13:17,306 --> 00:13:20,140
Certainly.

214
00:13:20,163 --> 00:13:23,322
Is the road crowded?

215
00:13:23,346 --> 00:13:27,312
It's a bit busy at this time.

216
00:13:27,335 --> 00:13:31,250
Will we make it in time for the flight?

217
00:13:31,274 --> 00:13:34,227
What time is your flight?

218
00:13:34,250 --> 00:13:37,089
Three o'clock.

219
00:13:37,113 --> 00:13:39,817
No problem.

220
00:13:39,841 --> 00:13:41,808
We'll make it.

221
00:13:41,831 --> 00:13:44,409
That's a relief.

222
00:13:44,432 --> 00:13:48,065
I'll load the luggage in the back.

223
00:13:48,088 --> 00:13:50,155
Thank you.

224
00:13:50,178 --> 00:13:54,312
Please be careful—it's heavy.

225
00:13:54,336 --> 00:13:57,269
Sure, I'll take care of it.

226
00:13:57,292 --> 00:14:00,559
Please fasten your seatbelt.

227
00:14:00,582 --> 00:14:02,772
Good idea.

228
00:14:02,795 --> 00:14:06,231
How's the air conditioning temperature?

229
00:14:06,254 --> 00:14:09,121
It's just right.

230
00:14:09,144 --> 00:14:10,644
Scene 8: Baggage Storage and Additional Fees

231
00:14:10,644 --> 00:14:12,999
Excuse me.

232
00:14:13,023 --> 00:14:16,799
I'd like to check my luggage.

233
00:14:16,822 --> 00:14:18,455
Sure.

234
00:14:18,478 --> 00:14:21,545
Please place it here.

235
00:14:21,568 --> 00:14:24,835
Is the weight okay?

236
00:14:24,858 --> 00:14:28,424
It's a bit heavy.

237
00:14:28,447 --> 00:14:31,924
Is it over the limit?

238
00:14:31,948 --> 00:14:33,919
Sure.

239
00:14:33,943 --> 00:14:36,935
It's 2 kilograms over.

240
00:14:36,958 --> 00:14:39,825
What should I do?

241
00:14:39,848 --> 00:14:44,516
You might want to pay an extra fee.

242
00:14:44,539 --> 00:14:47,447
How much will that be?

243
00:14:47,470 --> 00:14:50,704
It'll be 3,000 yen.

244
00:14:50,727 --> 00:14:53,704
That's expensive!

245
00:14:53,728 --> 00:14:58,228
How about removing some items?

246
00:14:58,251 --> 00:15:01,717
I'll take some things out.

247
00:15:01,740 --> 00:15:04,918
That would be better.

248
00:15:04,942 --> 00:15:07,617
I'll take out my laptop.

249
00:15:07,640 --> 00:15:12,174
You can bring your laptop on board.

250
00:15:12,197 --> 00:15:14,541
I'll take out some books too.

251
00:15:14,564 --> 00:15:18,031
Should I put them in my carry-on bag?

252
00:15:18,054 --> 00:15:20,843
Yes, please do.

253
00:15:20,866 --> 00:15:24,900
Let's weigh it again.

254
00:15:24,923 --> 00:15:27,396
How is it now?

255
00:15:27,420 --> 00:15:30,354
Perfect!

256
00:15:30,377 --> 00:15:32,849
I think we’re good.

257
00:15:32,872 --> 00:15:35,444
I'm glad you like it!

258
00:15:35,468 --> 00:15:39,773
I'll tag your carry-on as well.

259
00:15:39,797 --> 00:15:42,031
Thank you.

260
00:15:42,054 --> 00:15:46,120
Are there any fragile items inside?

261
00:15:46,143 --> 00:15:49,499
No, there aren't.

262
00:15:49,523 --> 00:15:53,259
Here's your ticket.

263
00:15:53,282 --> 00:15:55,653
Thank you very much.

264
00:15:55,677 --> 00:15:58,510
Have a wonderful trip!

265
00:15:58,534 --> 00:16:00,034
Scene 9: How to Tour a Museum Efficiently

266
00:16:00,034 --> 00:16:05,017
Excuse me, may I ask you something?

267
00:16:05,041 --> 00:16:08,347
Of course. How can I help?

268
00:16:08,370 --> 00:16:11,950
I'd like to look around the museum.

269
00:16:11,974 --> 00:16:15,168
Please take your time exploring.

270
00:16:15,191 --> 00:16:20,424
Actually, I only have an hour.

271
00:16:20,447 --> 00:16:24,314
That’s a bit tight on time.

272
00:16:24,338 --> 00:16:29,688
I want to see as much as possible efficiently. What should I do?

273
00:16:29,711 --> 00:16:34,011
You should focus on the famous paintings.

274
00:16:34,034 --> 00:16:37,934
Where can I find the famous paintings?

275
00:16:37,957 --> 00:16:41,858
They’re all gathered in the exhibition rooms on the second floor.

276
00:16:41,882 --> 00:16:46,257
How about starting from the second floor, then?

277
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:51,359
Yes, that route is highly recommended.

278
00:16:51,383 --> 00:16:54,616
What’s on the first floor?

279
00:16:54,639 --> 00:16:59,072
The first floor has older sculptures.

280
00:16:59,095 --> 00:17:02,680
I think I’ll skip the sculptures.

281
00:17:02,704 --> 00:17:07,371
In that case, please take the elevator to the second floor.

282
00:17:07,394 --> 00:17:10,660
Is the second floor spacious?

283
00:17:10,683 --> 00:17:13,950
It’s quite large, actually.

284
00:17:13,973 --> 00:17:17,289
I might get lost.

285
00:17:17,312 --> 00:17:21,286
You should take a pamphlet with you.

286
00:17:21,310 --> 00:17:25,011
Where can I get a pamphlet?

287
00:17:25,034 --> 00:17:28,701
They’re available at the counter near the entrance.

288
00:17:28,724 --> 00:17:30,857
Thank you very much.

289
00:17:30,880 --> 00:17:35,662
The famous paintings are marked with a red label.

290
00:17:35,685 --> 00:17:39,069
That makes it easy to spot them!

291
00:17:39,093 --> 00:17:42,449
May I take photos?

292
00:17:42,472 --> 00:17:45,985
Please refrain from taking photos.

293
00:17:46,009 --> 00:17:48,642
Got it.

294
00:17:48,665 --> 00:17:51,055
I’ll be careful.

295
00:17:51,078 --> 00:17:53,866
The exit is over there.

296
00:17:53,890 --> 00:17:57,223
Alright, I’ll be on my way.

297
00:17:57,246 --> 00:17:58,746
Scene 10: How to Enjoy Hot Springs

298
00:17:58,746 --> 00:18:04,046
I’d like to visit a hot spring around here.

299
00:18:04,069 --> 00:18:07,702
There are many hot springs to choose from.

300
00:18:07,725 --> 00:18:12,425
I’m looking for one I can visit for the day.

301
00:18:12,448 --> 00:18:18,428
There are hot springs near the station and others in the mountains.

302
00:18:18,452 --> 00:18:21,485
Which would you recommend?

303
00:18:21,508 --> 00:18:27,257
The mountain hot springs have beautiful scenery.

304
00:18:27,281 --> 00:18:32,581
But it seems like a lot of effort to walk there.

305
00:18:32,604 --> 00:18:36,670
You should use the shuttle bus.

306
00:18:36,693 --> 00:18:40,360
Is the shuttle bus free?

307
00:18:40,383 --> 00:18:44,085
Yes, it’s free of charge.

308
00:18:44,108 --> 00:18:46,942
That’s great to hear!

309
00:18:46,965 --> 00:18:52,231
You should ask about the bus schedule at the front desk.

310
00:18:52,254 --> 00:18:54,688
Got it.

311
00:18:54,711 --> 00:18:59,144
Are towels provided at the hot spring?

312
00:18:59,167 --> 00:19:03,743
You can rent towels, but there’s a fee.

313
00:19:03,767 --> 00:19:08,361
It’s better to bring your own towel.

314
00:19:08,384 --> 00:19:11,942
You’re right. I’ll bring one.

315
00:19:11,966 --> 00:19:17,274
Can I wear a swimsuit in the hot spring?

316
00:19:17,298 --> 00:19:22,365
Please do not wear swimsuits in Japanese hot springs.

317
00:19:22,388 --> 00:19:25,088
Got it.

318
00:19:25,111 --> 00:19:28,547
Where should I put my clothes?

319
00:19:28,571 --> 00:19:32,565
Please place them in the lockers in the changing room.

320
00:19:32,588 --> 00:19:36,339
Do the lockers have keys?

321
00:19:36,362 --> 00:19:41,796
Yes, they lock, so you can relax.

322
00:19:41,819 --> 00:19:46,685
You should wash your body before getting into the hot water.

323
00:19:46,708 --> 00:19:49,842
Right, it's just good manners.

324
00:19:49,865 --> 00:19:54,011
Do you have shampoo and soap?

325
00:19:54,034 --> 00:19:57,193
They're in the bath area.

326
00:19:57,217 --> 00:20:00,165
That's convenient!

327
00:20:00,188 --> 00:20:04,268
The water might be a little hot.

328
00:20:04,291 --> 00:20:07,558
I'll be careful when I get in.

329
00:20:07,581 --> 00:20:10,847
Take your time and enjoy.

330
00:20:20,878 --> 00:20:22,378
Scene 11: Choosing Souvenirs & Shelf Life

331
00:20:22,378 --> 00:20:24,845
Excuse me.

332
00:20:24,868 --> 00:20:28,607
I'd like to buy some souvenirs.

333
00:20:28,630 --> 00:20:30,943
Welcome. How can I help you?

334
00:20:30,967 --> 00:20:34,085
How about some traditional Japanese sweets?

335
00:20:34,109 --> 00:20:38,609
Do these sweets keep well?

336
00:20:38,632 --> 00:20:42,698
Please eat these today.

337
00:20:42,721 --> 00:20:47,266
I want to give them to friends tomorrow.

338
00:20:47,289 --> 00:20:51,607
In that case, how about these rice crackers?

339
00:20:51,631 --> 00:20:56,464
How long do the rice crackers last?

340
00:20:56,487 --> 00:21:00,154
They'll keep for about a month.

341
00:21:00,177 --> 00:21:02,810
That's perfect!

342
00:21:02,833 --> 00:21:07,391
If you prefer something sweet, we also have steamed buns.

343
00:21:07,415 --> 00:21:11,961
Do the steamed buns keep well?

344
00:21:11,984 --> 00:21:15,450
They'll last about a week.

345
00:21:15,473 --> 00:21:18,780
Then I'll take the steamed buns.

346
00:21:18,804 --> 00:21:21,782
How many would you like in a pack?

347
00:21:21,805 --> 00:21:26,001
I have five friends.

348
00:21:26,025 --> 00:21:29,925
We have packs of six and ten.

349
00:21:29,948 --> 00:21:33,490
I'll take the pack of six, then.

350
00:21:33,513 --> 00:21:37,389
That'll leave you with one extra. Is that okay?

351
00:21:37,413 --> 00:21:41,922
I'd like to eat one too, so that works out perfectly!

352
00:21:41,945 --> 00:21:44,281
Got it.

353
00:21:44,304 --> 00:21:46,873
A pack of six, then.

354
00:21:46,897 --> 00:21:50,073
Does it come in a box?

355
00:21:50,096 --> 00:21:52,162
Sure.

356
00:21:52,185 --> 00:21:55,419
Yes, it comes in a beautiful box.

357
00:21:55,442 --> 00:21:59,308
Could you wrap it in gift paper?

358
00:21:59,331 --> 00:22:01,235
Sure.

359
00:22:01,259 --> 00:22:03,595
Of course.

360
00:22:03,619 --> 00:22:07,162
Could you add a ribbon as well?

361
00:22:07,185 --> 00:22:09,497
Certainly.

362
00:22:09,521 --> 00:22:12,394
How much will that be?

363
00:22:12,417 --> 00:22:15,284
That'll be 1,200 yen.

364
00:22:15,307 --> 00:22:17,443
Thank you.

365
00:22:17,467 --> 00:22:20,448
Thank you very much.

366
00:22:20,471 --> 00:22:21,971
Scene 12: Workspace Usage Guide

367
00:22:21,971 --> 00:22:27,538
Excuse me, I'd like to do some work.

368
00:22:27,561 --> 00:22:31,428
Please use this lounge area.

369
00:22:31,451 --> 00:22:35,318
I'd like to use my laptop.

370
00:22:35,341 --> 00:22:39,675
You might prefer a seat with a power outlet.

371
00:22:39,698 --> 00:22:43,965
Do the seats by the window have power outlets?

372
00:22:43,988 --> 00:22:48,021
Yes, all seats have them.

373
00:22:48,044 --> 00:22:51,633
Is it okay to talk on the phone here?

374
00:22:51,656 --> 00:22:55,395
Please keep it quiet here.

375
00:22:55,419 --> 00:22:59,386
Where can I make a phone call?

376
00:22:59,409 --> 00:23:03,642
Please use the phone booth over there.

377
00:23:03,665 --> 00:23:06,499
Got it.

378
00:23:06,522 --> 00:23:10,064
Is the internet available here?

379
00:23:10,087 --> 00:23:14,521
Yes, we have free Wi-Fi.

380
00:23:14,544 --> 00:23:18,377
Could you tell me the password?

381
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:22,500
It's written on the card on the desk.

382
00:23:22,523 --> 00:23:24,762
Thank you very much.

383
00:23:24,785 --> 00:23:28,819
I'd like to print some documents.

384
00:23:28,842 --> 00:23:32,409
The copy machine is over there.

385
00:23:32,432 --> 00:23:36,298
I'm not sure how to use it.

386
00:23:36,321 --> 00:23:40,188
Please send the data from your computer.

387
00:23:40,211 --> 00:23:43,765
What do I do next?

388
00:23:43,788 --> 00:23:47,760
Just tap your card on the copy machine.

389
00:23:47,784 --> 00:23:51,650
Does it cost anything?

390
00:23:51,673 --> 00:23:55,707
Black and white prints are 10 yen per page.

391
00:23:55,730 --> 00:23:58,363
How about color prints?

392
00:23:58,386 --> 00:24:01,973
Color prints are 50 yen per page.

393
00:24:01,997 --> 00:24:05,781
I'll print in black and white then.

394
00:24:05,805 --> 00:24:10,438
Feel free to ask if you have any questions.

395
00:24:10,461 --> 00:24:13,328
Yes, I appreciate it.

396
00:24:13,351 --> 00:24:16,266
Take your time.

397
00:24:16,289 --> 00:24:17,789
Scene 13: How to Report Lost Items

398
00:24:17,789 --> 00:24:22,489
Excuse me, I think I lost my bag.

399
00:24:22,512 --> 00:24:25,615
Oh no, that’s terrible.

400
00:24:25,639 --> 00:24:28,874
Where did you lose it?

401
00:24:28,897 --> 00:24:32,888
I think it was in the station restroom.

402
00:24:32,911 --> 00:24:36,478
Did you check inside the restroom?

403
00:24:36,501 --> 00:24:40,368
Yes, but it wasn’t there.

404
00:24:40,391 --> 00:24:43,224
What does your bag look like?

405
00:24:43,247 --> 00:24:47,147
It’s a black leather bag.

406
00:24:47,170 --> 00:24:50,671
What was inside it?

407
00:24:50,695 --> 00:24:54,449
My wallet and passport.

408
00:24:54,472 --> 00:24:58,205
Those are important items.

409
00:24:58,228 --> 00:25:01,095
What should I do?

410
00:25:01,118 --> 00:25:05,855
You should fill out a lost property report.

411
00:25:05,878 --> 00:25:09,790
Could you show me how to fill it out?

412
00:25:09,814 --> 00:25:14,352
Sure. Please write your name and address here.

413
00:25:14,375 --> 00:25:18,042
Should I include my phone number too?

414
00:25:18,065 --> 00:25:22,565
Yes, please. We’ll need it to contact you.

415
00:25:22,588 --> 00:25:24,854
I’ve filled it out.

416
00:25:24,877 --> 00:25:28,511
We’ll call you if it’s found.

417
00:25:28,534 --> 00:25:31,446
When do you think it might be found?

418
00:25:31,469 --> 00:25:34,703
I’m not sure, unfortunately.

419
00:25:34,726 --> 00:25:38,959
Should I call the station myself?

420
00:25:38,982 --> 00:25:41,418
Good idea.

421
00:25:41,441 --> 00:25:45,193
You might want to call them tomorrow.

422
00:25:45,217 --> 00:25:49,927
Could you give me the station’s phone number?

423
00:25:49,950 --> 00:25:53,017
It’s written on this paper.

424
00:25:53,040 --> 00:25:55,473
Thank you very much.

425
00:25:55,496 --> 00:25:59,729
You should also cancel your credit cards.

426
00:25:59,752 --> 00:26:03,252
Yes, I’ll call them right away.

427
00:26:03,275 --> 00:26:06,209
I hope it’s found soon.

428
00:26:06,232 --> 00:26:09,404
Thank you so much for your help.

429
00:26:09,427 --> 00:26:12,927
Please take care on your way home.

430
00:26:12,950 --> 00:26:14,450
Scene 14: How to Choose a Rental Car

431
00:26:14,450 --> 00:26:19,969
Excuse me, I'd like to rent a car.

432
00:26:19,992 --> 00:26:23,359
Sure! What kind of car would you prefer?

433
00:26:23,382 --> 00:26:27,527
I'm planning a family road trip.

434
00:26:27,551 --> 00:26:30,251
How many people will be riding?

435
00:26:30,274 --> 00:26:32,807
Five of us.

436
00:26:32,830 --> 00:26:36,737
In that case, a minivan would be perfect.

437
00:26:36,761 --> 00:26:39,827
What about a regular car?

438
00:26:39,850 --> 00:26:43,960
A regular car might feel a bit cramped for five people.

439
00:26:43,983 --> 00:26:47,650
We also have a lot of luggage.

440
00:26:47,673 --> 00:26:51,381
Then a minivan it is!

441
00:26:51,405 --> 00:26:54,484
Is it easy to drive?

442
00:26:54,507 --> 00:26:59,007
Yes, the large windows make it very easy to see.

443
00:26:59,030 --> 00:27:02,297
Does it come with a navigation system?

444
00:27:02,320 --> 00:27:05,153
Yes, it does.

445
00:27:05,176 --> 00:27:09,276
I'm not sure how to use the navigation system.

446
00:27:09,299 --> 00:27:13,481
Why don’t you try entering the destination’s phone number?

447
00:27:13,505 --> 00:27:16,373
Can I use the address instead?

448
00:27:16,396 --> 00:27:20,429
Yes, you can search by address too.

449
00:27:20,452 --> 00:27:23,809
Can it give directions in English?

450
00:27:23,833 --> 00:27:27,509
You should change the language settings.

451
00:27:27,533 --> 00:27:30,500
Could you do that for me?

452
00:27:30,523 --> 00:27:34,789
Sure! I’ve just set it to English.

453
00:27:34,812 --> 00:27:37,052
Thank you very much.

454
00:27:37,075 --> 00:27:40,587
Do you have an ETC card?

455
00:27:40,611 --> 00:27:43,516
Yes, I do.

456
00:27:43,539 --> 00:27:47,206
Please insert it into the car’s ETC device.

457
00:27:47,229 --> 00:27:50,729
Should I refill the gas before returning the car?

458
00:27:50,752 --> 00:27:54,585
Yes, please return it with a full tank.

459
00:27:54,608 --> 00:27:58,320
Is there a gas station nearby?

460
00:27:58,343 --> 00:28:01,443
There’s one right in front of you.

461
00:28:01,466 --> 00:28:02,966
Scene 15: How to Purchase a Transportation Pass

462
00:28:02,966 --> 00:28:05,433
Excuse me.

463
00:28:05,456 --> 00:28:09,431
I’d like to ask for some advice.

464
00:28:09,455 --> 00:28:12,828
Of course. How can I help?

465
00:28:12,851 --> 00:28:17,318
I want to buy a one-day unlimited pass.

466
00:28:17,341 --> 00:28:20,657
For the bus only?

467
00:28:20,681 --> 00:28:22,947
Sure.

468
00:28:22,970 --> 00:28:25,885
Can I use it for the train as well?

469
00:28:25,909 --> 00:28:31,143
There’s a pass that covers both trains and buses.

470
00:28:31,166 --> 00:28:33,521
How much is it?

471
00:28:33,544 --> 00:28:36,848
It’s 1,500 yen.

472
00:28:36,872 --> 00:28:39,786
Where can I buy it?

473
00:28:39,809 --> 00:28:43,580
You can purchase it at this counter.

474
00:28:43,604 --> 00:28:47,305
Then I’ll take one, please.

475
00:28:47,329 --> 00:28:50,029
Certainly, thank you!

476
00:28:50,052 --> 00:28:53,985
I’d like to visit the castle and the art museum.

477
00:28:54,008 --> 00:28:57,885
The castle is very crowded, though.

478
00:28:57,909 --> 00:29:01,609
I’d rather avoid crowds.

479
00:29:01,632 --> 00:29:05,498
It’s best to go early in the morning.

480
00:29:05,521 --> 00:29:08,291
What about in the afternoon?

481
00:29:08,315 --> 00:29:12,593
The art museum would be a better choice in the afternoon.

482
00:29:12,616 --> 00:29:17,728
How do I get from the castle to the art museum?

483
00:29:17,752 --> 00:29:22,218
Just take Bus No. 3 using this pass.

484
00:29:22,241 --> 00:29:25,675
Will it take long?

485
00:29:25,698 --> 00:29:28,998
It’ll take about 10 minutes.

486
00:29:29,021 --> 00:29:33,921
Are there any restaurants around the art museum?

487
00:29:33,944 --> 00:29:35,821
Sure.

488
00:29:35,845 --> 00:29:39,346
There are plenty of great places to eat.

489
00:29:39,369 --> 00:29:43,469
Could you recommend a good one?

490
00:29:43,493 --> 00:29:48,793
I recommend the place marked with a red star on this map.

491
00:29:48,816 --> 00:29:50,949
Thank you very much.

492
00:29:50,972 --> 00:29:55,639
Please be mindful of the bus schedule on your way back.

493
00:29:55,662 --> 00:29:58,581
What time is the last bus?

494
00:29:58,604 --> 00:30:01,355
It's at 8 o'clock.

495
00:30:01,378 --> 00:30:04,336
Have a great time!

496
00:30:04,359 --> 00:30:05,859
Scene 16: How to Prepare Matcha

497
00:30:05,859 --> 00:30:08,826
Excuse me.

498
00:30:08,849 --> 00:30:13,416
I'd like to try making matcha.

499
00:30:13,439 --> 00:30:19,110
Sure, please have a seat here.

500
00:30:19,133 --> 00:30:23,603
It's my first time—is that okay?

501
00:30:23,626 --> 00:30:29,763
Yes, don't worry. I'll guide you through it.

502
00:30:29,786 --> 00:30:33,453
Where should I start?

503
00:30:33,476 --> 00:30:37,809
First, please enjoy this sweet treat.

504
00:30:37,832 --> 00:30:41,366
It's sweet and delicious!

505
00:30:41,389 --> 00:30:45,762
Next, we'll prepare the matcha.

506
00:30:45,785 --> 00:30:49,485
We use this tool, right?

507
00:30:49,508 --> 00:30:53,442
Yes, it's called a *chasen* (tea whisk).

508
00:30:53,465 --> 00:30:56,966
How should I whisk it?

509
00:30:56,989 --> 00:31:01,856
Try keeping your wrist relaxed and whisk gently.

510
00:31:01,879 --> 00:31:04,866
Like this?

511
00:31:04,890 --> 00:31:08,672
How about whisking a little faster?

512
00:31:08,695 --> 00:31:13,068
The foam isn't forming well.

513
00:31:13,092 --> 00:31:17,080
Move it straight back and forth.

514
00:31:17,104 --> 00:31:22,700
Oh, some foam is starting to form!

515
00:31:22,723 --> 00:31:26,321
You did a great job!

516
00:31:26,345 --> 00:31:29,494
Can I drink it now?

517
00:31:29,517 --> 00:31:34,684
Yes, hold the bowl with both hands and enjoy.

518
00:31:34,707 --> 00:31:39,807
It's a bit bitter, but it tastes good.

519
00:31:39,830 --> 00:31:44,004
There's something special about tea you prepare yourself.

520
00:31:44,027 --> 00:31:48,372
I'd like to buy this whisk to take home.

521
00:31:48,396 --> 00:31:52,365
They sell them at the shop over there.

522
00:31:52,389 --> 00:31:57,555
How should I store it at home?

523
00:31:57,578 --> 00:32:03,011
After washing, it's best to stand it on a holder.

524
00:32:03,034 --> 00:32:06,668
Do you sell the holder too?

525
00:32:06,691 --> 00:32:11,273
Yes, it's a good idea to buy them together.

526
00:32:11,296 --> 00:32:14,632
Will it lose its shape?

527
00:32:14,655 --> 00:32:19,922
No, using a holder will help it last longer.

528
00:32:19,945 --> 00:32:21,445
Scene 17: Consulting About Hotel Meals

529
00:32:21,445 --> 00:32:26,001
Excuse me, are you from the front desk?

530
00:32:26,024 --> 00:32:30,058
Yes, welcome. How may I assist you?

531
00:32:30,081 --> 00:32:35,015
I'd like to discuss dinner timing.

532
00:32:35,038 --> 00:32:39,355
Dinner is scheduled for 6 o'clock.

533
00:32:39,379 --> 00:32:44,748
Could we have it a little later?

534
00:32:44,771 --> 00:32:48,871
7 o'clock works fine.

535
00:32:48,894 --> 00:32:52,994
Then, let's make it 7 o'clock, please.

536
00:32:53,017 --> 00:32:55,684
Certainly.

537
00:32:55,707 --> 00:33:00,612
Also, I wanted to ask about the meal itself.

538
00:33:00,636 --> 00:33:05,136
Is there an issue with the menu?

539
00:33:05,159 --> 00:33:09,392
I have a shrimp allergy.

540
00:33:09,415 --> 00:33:13,848
I'm glad you told me that early.

541
00:33:13,871 --> 00:33:18,217
I'd like to avoid eating shrimp, if possible.

542
00:33:18,241 --> 00:33:22,941
We should remove shrimp from the menu, then.

543
00:33:22,964 --> 00:33:26,831
Do you have any alternative dishes?

544
00:33:26,854 --> 00:33:31,087
Yes, how about crab?

545
00:33:31,110 --> 00:33:35,250
I'm a little wary of crab too, though.

546
00:33:35,274 --> 00:33:40,307
In that case, how about switching to a fish dish?

547
00:33:40,330 --> 00:33:44,463
Fish is fine with me.

548
00:33:44,486 --> 00:33:48,403
Then I'll prepare grilled fish for you.

549
00:33:48,427 --> 00:33:52,661
Thank you so much. That really helps.

550
00:33:52,685 --> 00:33:56,662
Is there anything else you can't eat?

551
00:33:56,685 --> 00:34:00,518
No, everything else is fine.

552
00:34:00,541 --> 00:34:03,775
Would you like some alcohol?

553
00:34:03,798 --> 00:34:08,187
I'd love to try some local wine.

554
00:34:08,210 --> 00:34:11,943
You can order it at the restaurant.

555
00:34:11,966 --> 00:34:14,485
Got it.

556
00:34:14,508 --> 00:34:18,342
Have you taken a bath yet?

557
00:34:18,365 --> 00:34:21,298
I'm about to take one now.

558
00:34:21,321 --> 00:34:25,421
Please relax and enjoy your bath.

559
00:34:25,444 --> 00:34:26,944
Scene 18: Shipping Packages – How to Send via EMS

560
00:34:26,944 --> 00:34:29,418
Excuse me.

561
00:34:29,441 --> 00:34:33,274
I'd like to send a package.

562
00:34:33,297 --> 00:34:36,231
Where would you like to send it?

563
00:34:36,254 --> 00:34:40,163
To New York in the U.S.

564
00:34:40,186 --> 00:34:43,119
What’s inside?

565
00:34:43,142 --> 00:34:47,847
Books, clothes, and some snacks.

566
00:34:47,871 --> 00:34:51,304
Are the snacks okay to send?

567
00:34:51,327 --> 00:34:56,667
I don’t think there’s any meat, so it should be fine.

568
00:34:56,691 --> 00:35:00,124
How soon would you like it delivered?

569
00:35:00,147 --> 00:35:04,862
As soon as possible, please.

570
00:35:04,885 --> 00:35:09,865
Then I recommend using EMS.

571
00:35:09,888 --> 00:35:15,064
How many days does EMS take?

572
00:35:15,088 --> 00:35:18,994
It arrives in about 3 to 4 days.

573
00:35:19,018 --> 00:35:21,772
How much will it cost?

574
00:35:21,795 --> 00:35:25,704
Let me weigh it for you.

575
00:35:25,727 --> 00:35:27,861
Thank you.

576
00:35:27,884 --> 00:35:32,393
It’s 3 kilograms, so that’ll be 5,000 yen.

577
00:35:32,416 --> 00:35:35,883
Can I send it in this box?

578
00:35:35,906 --> 00:35:40,224
The box seems a little flimsy.

579
00:35:40,247 --> 00:35:44,953
It might break—what should I do?

580
00:35:44,976 --> 00:35:50,043
You should reinforce it with packing tape.

581
00:35:50,066 --> 00:35:54,766
Could I borrow some packing tape?

582
00:35:54,789 --> 00:35:58,422
Sure, go ahead and use it.

583
00:35:58,445 --> 00:36:02,215
Should I tape the corners too?

584
00:36:02,239 --> 00:36:06,939
Yes, those spots tear easily.

585
00:36:06,962 --> 00:36:11,079
Should I write the address on this paper?

586
00:36:11,102 --> 00:36:15,449
Yes, please write it in English.

587
00:36:15,473 --> 00:36:19,773
Should I list the value of the contents too?

588
00:36:19,797 --> 00:36:23,907
Yes, please write it accurately.

589
00:36:23,930 --> 00:36:26,306
I’ve filled it out.

590
00:36:26,330 --> 00:36:28,881
I appreciate your help.

591
00:36:28,905 --> 00:36:32,700
Sure, I'll take care of it.

592
00:36:32,723 --> 00:36:34,223
Scene 19: Asking for Help – Requesting Assistance

593
00:36:34,223 --> 00:36:36,789
Excuse me.

594
00:36:36,812 --> 00:36:40,046
Do you have a moment?

595
00:36:40,069 --> 00:36:44,135
Yes, what can I do for you?

596
00:36:44,158 --> 00:36:48,393
I'd like to put my luggage on the overhead rack.

597
00:36:48,417 --> 00:36:51,083
That looks heavy.

598
00:36:51,106 --> 00:36:56,418
Yeah, I can't lift it by myself.

599
00:36:56,442 --> 00:36:59,175
Need a hand?

600
00:36:59,198 --> 00:37:01,770
Excuse me.

601
00:37:01,794 --> 00:37:04,927
Would you mind helping me?

602
00:37:04,950 --> 00:37:07,617
Sure, no problem.

603
00:37:07,640 --> 00:37:10,274
On three. One, two, three!

604
00:37:10,297 --> 00:37:13,003
Thank you very much.

605
00:37:13,027 --> 00:37:15,620
Thanks so much!

606
00:37:15,643 --> 00:37:19,616
Don't mention it!

607
00:37:19,640 --> 00:37:23,190
Where are you seated?

608
00:37:23,213 --> 00:37:27,953
I'm in the seat right in front of you.

609
00:37:27,976 --> 00:37:30,443
I see.

610
00:37:30,466 --> 00:37:33,099
Excuse me.

611
00:37:33,122 --> 00:37:36,955
Do you mind if I recline my seat a little?

612
00:37:36,978 --> 00:37:40,412
Here you go.

613
00:37:40,435 --> 00:37:42,868
Will that be too cramped for you?

614
00:37:42,891 --> 00:37:46,524
No, I'm fine.

615
00:37:46,547 --> 00:37:51,014
Let me know if it gets uncomfortable, okay?

616
00:37:51,038 --> 00:37:53,408
Thank you very much.

617
00:37:53,431 --> 00:37:57,386
The view outside is beautiful, isn't it?

618
00:37:57,410 --> 00:38:01,910
We should be able to see Mt. Fuji soon.

619
00:38:01,933 --> 00:38:07,504
Which side will it be on, left or right?

620
00:38:07,528 --> 00:38:11,828
I think it'll be on the right side.

621
00:38:11,851 --> 00:38:15,045
I'd love to take a photo.

622
00:38:15,068 --> 00:38:19,368
Why not open the window blind?

623
00:38:19,391 --> 00:38:21,658
Good idea.

624
00:38:21,681 --> 00:38:24,581
Won't it be too bright?

625
00:38:24,604 --> 00:38:28,137
No, it's fine.

626
00:38:28,160 --> 00:38:32,793
Oh, look! There's Mt. Fuji!

627
00:38:32,816 --> 00:38:35,350
Wow, you're right!

628
00:38:35,373 --> 00:38:38,073
It's so beautiful.

629
00:38:38,096 --> 00:38:41,796
This is going to be a great trip!

630
00:38:41,818 --> 00:38:43,318
Scene 20: Photo-Taking Conversations / Basic Japanese for Taking Photos

631
00:38:43,318 --> 00:38:45,891
Excuse me.

632
00:38:45,915 --> 00:38:50,015
Could you take a photo for me, please?

633
00:38:50,038 --> 00:38:53,304
Sure, I'd be happy to.

634
00:38:53,327 --> 00:38:56,102
Could you pass me the camera?

635
00:38:56,126 --> 00:38:59,715
Just press this button.

636
00:38:59,738 --> 00:39:03,305
What should I use as the background?

637
00:39:03,328 --> 00:39:08,228
I'd like to get the whole castle in the shot.

638
00:39:08,251 --> 00:39:13,284
In that case, you should step back a little more.

639
00:39:13,307 --> 00:39:16,222
Around here?

640
00:39:16,246 --> 00:39:19,982
Yes, that spot is perfect.

641
00:39:20,005 --> 00:39:23,471
How should I pose?

642
00:39:23,494 --> 00:39:27,470
A little smile would be nice.

643
00:39:27,494 --> 00:39:31,194
Should I do a peace sign?

644
00:39:31,217 --> 00:39:35,753
Yeah, that would look fun and great!

645
00:39:35,776 --> 00:39:38,488
Okay, go ahead and take it.

646
00:39:38,512 --> 00:39:42,412
Alright, say cheese!

647
00:39:42,435 --> 00:39:44,535
How does it look?

648
00:39:44,558 --> 00:39:47,331
Did it turn out okay?

649
00:39:47,355 --> 00:39:50,667
It's a bit backlit.

650
00:39:50,690 --> 00:39:54,223
Our faces are coming out dark.

651
00:39:54,246 --> 00:39:57,802
Should we change direction?

652
00:39:57,826 --> 00:40:03,224
Yes, why not stand to the right of the castle?

653
00:40:03,248 --> 00:40:07,781
Okay, I'll stand to the right of the castle.

654
00:40:07,804 --> 00:40:13,193
That should give you better lighting and a nicer shot!

655
00:40:13,217 --> 00:40:15,891
One more, please.

656
00:40:15,914 --> 00:40:19,214
Sure, I'll take it.

657
00:40:19,237 --> 00:40:22,341
Can I check it?

658
00:40:22,364 --> 00:40:25,431
Go ahead, take a look.

659
00:40:25,454 --> 00:40:29,799
Wow, this turned out so beautiful!

660
00:40:29,823 --> 00:40:32,365
I'm glad you like it!

661
00:40:32,388 --> 00:40:36,021
Let me take a photo of you too.

662
00:40:36,044 --> 00:40:38,360
Really?

663
00:40:38,384 --> 00:40:40,860
Thank you very much.

664
00:40:40,884 --> 00:40:45,551
I'll make sure the castle looks great in the shot.

665
00:40:45,574 --> 00:40:48,523
I appreciate your help.